content.text:
The bindings for the target_user role should contain only the resolved match, not the admin namesake. Fixing the bindings key.

```json
{
  "seed_edits": [],
  "bindings": {
    "target_user": ["U05MORGAN23"],
    "admin_namesake": ["U07MORGANFREE"],
    "target_channel": ["C02EFGH5678"],
    "acting_user": ["U01AGENBOT9"],
    "unrelated_member_of_random": [
      {"channel_id":"C02EFGH5678","user_id":"U03ROBERT23"},
      {"channel_id":"C02EFGH5678","user_id":"U06HUBERT23"}
    ]
  },
  "selectors": [
    {
      "root_table": "users",
      "scope": [],
      "focal": {
        "path": ["users","user_teams"],
        "joins": ["user_teams.user_id"],
        "filters": [
          {"node":0,"field":"real_name","op":"contains_ci","value":"Morgan"},
          {"node":1,"field":"team_id","op":"eq","value":"T01WORKSPACE"},
          {"node":1,"field":"role","op":"ne","value":"admin"}
        ]
      },
      "auxiliary": []
    },
    {
      "root_table": "channels",
      "scope": [],
      "focal": {
        "path": ["channels"],
        "joins": [],
        "filters": [
          {"node":0,"field":"channel_name","op":"eq","value":"random"},
          {"node":0,"field":"team_id","op":"eq","value":"T01WORKSPACE"}
        ]
      },
      "auxiliary": []
    }
  ],
  "negative_referents": ["U07MORGANFREE"],
  "notes": "Corrected: target_user binding now holds only the resolved non-admin Morgan (U05MORGAN23), matching the O1 selector's single computed match. The admin namesake U07MORGANFREE remains bound separately under its own role (admin_namesake) and is listed as a negative referent, not as part of the target_user resolution. No seed edits were needed: the base seed already contains both Morgan-named users, the target channel #random (C02EFGH5678), and the acting bot U01AGENBOT9 already a member of both the workspace and #random."
}
```
